PATCH 180: base-loss fix for the per-node display-list PAINT handler FUN_0000_4937 (asm 0x4937).

4937 is dispatched by 209e's display-list walk via `fist_icall_near(0x0,off)()` with NO register args.
Its first statement (asm `mov si,[bx+2] ; movb ss:[bp+si],3`) needs bx (the node offset) and bp (the
walk base), which Ghidra emitted as dropped params param_1/param_2 -> `*(int*)(param_1+2)` was a wild
host deref (SIGSEGV, param_1=0).  209e already publishes bx to DGROUP:0x3e08 and bp to g_fist_paintbp
(patch 142); read them here.  SS=DGROUP so [bp+si] is DGROUP-relative.  The rest of the body already
uses correct DAT_ accessors.

Reached only on the ACCEPT mission cascade (the menu's display-list nodes never select the 4937 paint
method, else the pre-patch wild deref would crash the 19 flows -> they are 19/19) -> behaviour-neutral.
Sources stay pristine; fist.c via build/.

--- a/fist.c	2026-07-11 03:02:50.709295122 +0200
+++ b/fist.c	2026-07-11 03:03:00.639715220 +0200
@@ -13641,8 +13641,20 @@
 
 {
   byte bVar1;
-  
-  *(undefined1 *)(param_2 + *(int *)(param_1 + 2)) = 3;
+
+  /* PATCH 180: base-loss fix (asm 0x4937: `mov si,[bx+2] ; movb ss:[bp+si],3`).  4937 is a per-node
+     display-list PAINT handler dispatched by 209e's walk via `fist_icall_near(0x0,off)()` with NO args,
+     so its bx (node offset) / bp (walk base) register inputs were dropped -> param_1/param_2 = garbage ->
+     `*(int*)(param_1+2)` wild-deref (SIGSEGV, param_1=0).  209e publishes bx to DGROUP:0x3e08 and bp to
+     g_fist_paintbp (patch 142); read them here.  SS=DGROUP so [bp+si] is DGROUP-relative. */
+  {
+    extern unsigned short g_fist_paintbp;
+    uint8_t *dg = g_mem + 0x1c000;
+    uint16_t bx = *(uint16_t *)(dg + 0x3e08);
+    uint16_t bp = g_fist_paintbp;
+    uint16_t si = *(uint16_t *)(dg + (uint16_t)(bx + 2));
+    *(uint8_t *)(dg + (uint16_t)(bp + si)) = 3;
+  }
   bVar1 = DAT_1000_d548;
   if ((DAT_2000_3c08 == 2) || (DAT_2000_3a40 != 0)) {
     return;
